🧠 Introduction

Building a RAG system is not enough.

👉 We must also evaluate:

✔ Retrieval quality
✔ Answer quality
✔ Grounding accuracy
✔ Hallucination rate

RAG evaluation helps measure how well the system performs.

---

🎯 Why RAG Evaluation Matters

Without evaluation:

❌ Poor retrieval may go unnoticed
❌ Hallucinations may increase
❌ Wrong answers may appear correct

---

🔄 RAG Evaluation Pipeline

```text id="evaluation_flow"
User Query → Retrieval → Context → LLM Response → Evaluation Metrics
```

---

📌 What Do We Evaluate?

Two major components:

| Component | What to Evaluate                |
| --------- | ------------------------------- |
| Retriever | Relevance of retrieved chunks   |
| Generator | Correctness of generated answer |

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔍 1. Precision

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 Definition

```text id="precision_def"
Measures how many retrieved documents are actually relevant
```

---

📊 Formula

```text id="precision_formula"
Precision = Relevant Retrieved / Total Retrieved
```

---

📌 Example

Retriever returns 5 chunks:

* 4 relevant
* 1 irrelevant

```text id="precision_example"
Precision = 4 / 5 = 0.8
```

---

🎯 High Precision Means

✔ Less irrelevant information
✔ Cleaner retrieval results

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔍 2. Recall

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 Definition

```text id="recall_def"
Measures how many relevant documents were successfully retrieved
```

---

📊 Formula

```text id="recall_formula"
Recall = Relevant Retrieved / Total Relevant Documents
```

---

📌 Example

There are 10 relevant chunks in database.

Retriever finds 7.

```text id="recall_example"
Recall = 7 / 10 = 0.7
```

---

🎯 High Recall Means

✔ Important information is not missed
✔ Better coverage

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚖️ 3. F1 Score

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 Definition

```text id="f1_def"
Harmonic mean of Precision and Recall
```

---

📊 Formula

```text id="f1_formula"
F1 = 2 × (Precision × Recall) / (Precision + Recall)
```

---

🎯 Why F1 is Important

Balances:

✔ Precision
✔ Recall

Useful when both metrics matter equally.

---

📊 Precision vs Recall

| Metric    | Focus                        |
| --------- | ---------------------------- |
| Precision | Quality of retrieved results |
| Recall    | Coverage of relevant results |
| F1 Score  | Balance between both         |

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🤖 4. Ragas Framework

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is Ragas?

```text id="ragas_def"
An evaluation framework specifically designed for RAG systems
```

---

🔹 Why Use Ragas?

✔ Automated RAG evaluation
✔ Measures retrieval + generation quality
✔ Easy integration with LangChain

---

📊 Metrics Supported by Ragas

| Metric            | Purpose                        |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Faithfulness      | Is answer grounded in context? |
| Answer Relevancy  | Does answer match question?    |
| Context Precision | Quality of retrieved chunks    |
| Context Recall    | Coverage of retrieved chunks   |

---

💻 Installation

```bash id="ragas_install"
pip install ragas
```

---

💻 Example Usage

```python id="ragas_example"
from ragas import evaluate

results = evaluate(
    dataset=dataset,
    metrics=[
        faithfulness,
        answer_relevancy,
        context_precision,
        context_recall
    ]
)

print(results)
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔥 Faithfulness Metric

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is Faithfulness?

```text id="faithfulness_def"
Measures whether the answer is supported by retrieved context
```

---

📌 Example

If model invents information:

❌ Low faithfulness

If answer is fully grounded:

✅ High faithfulness

---

🚨 Hallucination Detection

RAG evaluation helps detect hallucinations.

Hallucination:

```text id="hallucination_def"
Generating information not supported by retrieved documents
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔧 Best Practices for RAG Evaluation

✔ Evaluate both retrieval and generation
✔ Use high-quality test queries
✔ Monitor hallucination rate
✔ Tune chunking and retriever settings

---

🌍 Real-World Applications

✔ Enterprise search systems
✔ Medical assistants
✔ Legal AI systems
✔ Customer support chatbots

---

🧠 Interview Answer (Simple)

> Precision measures retrieval accuracy, recall measures retrieval coverage, and F1 balances both. Ragas is a framework used to evaluate RAG systems for retrieval quality, faithfulness, and answer relevance.

